<br clear="all" style="page-break-before:always;">


<div style="font-family:Times New Roman;">

<p style="margin:0in 0in .0001pt;text-indent:.5in;"><font size="2" face="Times New Roman" style="font-size:10.0pt;">&nbsp;</font></p>

<p style="margin:0in 0in .0001pt;text-indent:.5in;"><i><font size="2" face="Times New Roman" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-style:italic;">Parties.&#160; </font></i><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">The Columbia
Project is owned by West Columbia Pike, LLC (&#147;Columbia Project Owner&#148;), which
is solely owned by Fairfield Columbia Pike Limited Partnership (&#147;Columbia
Investment Partnership&#148;).&#160; Columbia
Investment Partnership is owned by affiliates of Fairfield Residential, LLC (&#147;Fairfield
Residential&#148;), the developer of the project, and by Behringer Harvard Columbia
REIT, LLC (&#147;Columbia REIT&#148;).&#160; We refer to
the Fairfield Residential affiliates that are the partners in Columbia
Investment Partnership as the &#147;Columbia Developer Partners.&#148;&#160; The general partner of Columbia Investment
Partnership (&#147;Columbia GP&#148;) is one of the Columbia Developer Partners.</font></p>

<p style="margin:0in 0in .0001pt;text-indent:.5in;"><font size="2" face="Times New Roman" style="font-size:10.0pt;">&nbsp;</font></p>



<p style="margin:0in 0in .0001pt;text-indent:.5in;"><font size="2" face="Times New Roman" style="font-size:10.0pt;">All of the voting interests
and 99% of the economic interests in Columbia REIT are currently owned by, and
Columbia REIT is managed by, Behringer Harvard Columbia Venture, LLC (&#147;Columbia
Venture&#148;), the entity through which we and our Co-Investment Partner are
investing in Columbia Project Owner.&#160;
Columbia Venture is managed by us and owned 55% by us and 45% by our
Co-Investment Partner.&#160; In addition to
making our equity investment in the Columbia Project through Columbia REIT, we
and our Co-Investment Partner are also making the mezzanine loan through
Columbia REIT.</font></p>



<p style="margin:0in 0in .0001pt;text-indent:.5in;"><font size="2" face="Times New Roman" style="font-size:10.0pt;">&nbsp;</font></p>

<p style="margin:0in 0in .0001pt;text-indent:.5in;"><i><font size="2" face="Times New Roman" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-style:italic;">Senior Financing and Total Projected Development Costs.&#160; </font></i><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">The Columbia Project serves
as collateral for a construction loan from Key Bank National Association (&#147;Columbia</font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">  </font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">Senior Lender&#148;)
to Columbia Project Owner for approximately </font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">$69,842,000</font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">.&#160; The senior loan will not be funded until all
principal under the mezzanine loan has been funded.&#160; The anticipated total development cost of the
Columbia Project is $99,774,000.&#160; The
equity investment by us and our Co-Investment Partner in the Columbia Project
represents approximately 3.56%<b>  </b>of this cost
and the mezzanine loan investment by us and our Co-Investment Partner in the
Columbia Project will finance approximately 20% of this cost.</font></p>

<p style="margin:0in 0in .0001pt;text-indent:.5in;"><font size="2" face="Times New Roman" style="font-size:10.0pt;">&nbsp;</font></p>



<p style="margin:0in 0in .0001pt;text-indent:.55in;"><i><font size="2" face="Times New Roman" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-style:italic;">Project Equity/Columbia
Investment Partnership Capital Contributions.&#160;
</font></i><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">The owners of the Columbia Project have contributed $3,553,000 in cash
to the project<i>.&#160;&#160; </i>Columbia
REIT&#146;s $3,553,000 equity investment was made in the form of a capital
contribution to Columbia Investment Partnership, which contribution constitutes
100% of the initial capital contributed to the partnership.&#160; Pursuant to the provisions of the partnership
agreement, Columbia REIT&#146;s pro-rata share of any additional capital
contributions required by the partnership is 70% of such additional capital
while that of the Columbia Developer Partners is 30%. </font></p>



<p style="margin:0in 0in .0001pt;text-indent:.55in;"><font size="2" face="Times New Roman" style="font-size:10.0pt;">&nbsp;</font></p>

<p style="margin:0in 0in .0001pt;text-indent:.55in;"><i><font size="2" face="Times New Roman" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-style:italic;">Columbia Investment Partnership Distributions. </font></i><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">Pursuant to the
provisions of the Columbia Investment Partnership, distributions are made
generally as follows: (i)&nbsp;first, to pay all partners a preferred return of
14%, compounded quarterly, on their undistributed first-priority capital (i.e.,
capital paid on a non-pro-rata basis to fund unexpected project shortfalls); (ii)&nbsp;second,
to each partner for any undistributed first-priority capital; (iii)&nbsp;third,
to pay all partners a preferred return of 9.5%, compounded quarterly, on their
undistributed second-priority capital (i.e., capital other than first-priority
capital); (iv)&nbsp;fourth, to return undistributed second-priority capital to
the respective partners; (v)&nbsp;fifth, to affiliates of the Columbia
Developer Partner to the extent of the accrued and unpaid deferred fees
(discussed below); (vi)&nbsp;sixth, 1% to the general partner, 29% to the
limited partners (other than Columbia REIT) and 70% to Columbia REIT (but only
until Columbia REIT receives a return of all its capital contributions plus a
cumulative, monthly compounded, return at a rate of 12% per annum on such
capital contributions); (vii)&nbsp;seventh, 1% to the general partner, 39% to
the limited partners (other than Columbia REIT) and 60% to Columbia REIT (but
only until Columbia REIT receives a return of all its capital contributions
plus a cumulative, monthly compounded, return at a rate of 15% per annum on
such capital contributions); and (viii)&nbsp;thereafter, to pay the partners
the net proceeds in accordance with their respective back-end percentage
interests, which are 49.9% for the Columbia Developer Partners and 50.1% for
Columbia REIT, but may be adjusted in the event of a partner&#146;s failure to make
additional capital contributions when required.&#160;
If Columbia REIT exercises the Columbia Option (discussed below), the
respective back-end percentage interests of the partners of Columbia Investment
Partnership will remain: (1)&nbsp;the Columbia Developer Partners &#151; 49.9%, and (2)&nbsp;Columbia
REIT &#151; 50.1%.</font></p>

<p style="margin:0in 0in .0001pt;text-indent:.55in;"><font size="2" face="Times New Roman" style="font-size:10.0pt;">&nbsp;</font></p>

<p style="margin:0in 0in .0001pt;text-indent:.55in;"><i><font size="2" face="Times New Roman" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-style:italic;">Columbia Developer Partners&#146; Deferred Fees.</font></i><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">&#160; Affiliates of the Columbia Developer Partners
will receive payment of the following deferred fees after completion of the
project and from any net distributable cash remaining after distributions (i)&nbsp;through
(iv)&nbsp;described above are made to the partners: (i)&nbsp;a development fee
equal to 3% of the lesser of the total Columbia Project costs set forth in the
budget or those actually incurred in developing the Columbia Project; (ii)&nbsp;a
general contractor&#146;s fee equal to 6% of the lesser of hard construction costs
set forth in the budget or those actually incurred in developing the Columbia
Project; (iii)&nbsp;an acquisition fee of $93,600 payable to </font></p>

<p style="margin:0in 0in .0001pt;text-indent:.55in;"><font size="2" face="Times New Roman" style="font-size:10.0pt;">&nbsp;</font></p>

<p align="center" style="margin:0in 0in .0001pt;text-align:center;"><font size="2" face="Times New Roman" style="font-size:10.0pt;">&nbsp;</font></p>

<p align="center" style="margin:0in 0in .0001pt;text-align:center;"><font size="2" face="Times New Roman" style="font-size:10.0pt;">153</font></p>

<div style="margin:0in 0in .0001pt;"><hr size="3" width="100%" noshade color="#010101" align="left"></div>

</div>
<!-- SEQ.=1,FOLIO='153',FILE='C:\JMS\eudelhofen\07-31961-1\task2929810\31961-1-bd-33.htm',USER='eudelho',CD='May  9 15:53 2008' -->


<br clear="all" style="page-break-before:always;">


<div style="font-family:Times New Roman;">

<p align="center" style="margin:0in 0in .0001pt;text-align:center;"><font size="2" face="Times New Roman" style="font-size:10.0pt;">&nbsp;</font></p>

<p style="margin:0in 0in .0001pt;"><font size="2" face="Times New Roman" style="font-size:10.0pt;">employees
or consultants of Columbia GP; (iv)&nbsp;a capital markets fee of $175,000
payable to employees or consultants of Columbia GP; and (v)&nbsp;a disposition
fee payable upon closing of the sale of the Columbia Project of 1% of the gross
sales price, reduced by any fee paid to a third-party broker (except a
disposition fee shall not be payable in case of a sale under the call right,
put right or buy/sell provisions discussed below).</font></p>

<p style="margin:0in 0in .0001pt;text-indent:.55in;"><font size="2" face="Times New Roman" style="font-size:10.0pt;">&nbsp;</font></p>

<p style="margin:0in 0in .0001pt;text-indent:.55in;"><i><font size="2" face="Times New Roman" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-style:italic;">Columbia Developer Partners&#146; Other Fees.</font></i><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">&#160; An affiliate of the Columbia Developer
Partners will receive a property management fee equal to the greater of 2% of
gross proceeds collected from the Columbia Project per month or $5,000.&#160; A development processing fee of $234,000 was paid
to employees or consultants of Columbia GP at closing.</font></p>

<p style="margin:0in 0in .0001pt;text-indent:.55in;"><font size="2" face="Times New Roman" style="font-size:10.0pt;">&nbsp;</font></p>

<p style="margin:0in 0in .0001pt;text-indent:.55in;"><i><font size="2" face="Times New Roman" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-style:italic;">Mezzanine Loan Terms.&#160; </font></i><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">The aggregate
principal amount of the mezzanine loan is $</font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">19,955,000 </font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">and will accrue
interest at the rate of 9.5% per annum.&#160;
In connection with the closing of the mezzanine loan, the parties have
agreed or will agree to a completion date, a construction budget and
construction plans for the project.&#160; No
changes to such completion date, construction budget or construction plans may
be made without Columbia</font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;"> REIT&#146;s </font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">consent, except (i)&nbsp;completion
date extensions due to &#147;acts of God,&#148; (ii)&nbsp;certain reallocations of
amounts among the line items of the budget, and (iii)&nbsp;changes to amounts
in the budget that, individually, do not increase or decrease the project costs
by more than $100,000 and, in the aggregate, do not increase the project costs
or decrease the project costs by more than $500,000.&#160; Columbia</font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;"> REIT also has the right to
approve all contractors (except the general contractor) and all construction
contracts with such contractors except for those that do not exceed $100,000.</font></p>

<p style="margin:0in 0in .0001pt;text-indent:.55in;"><font size="2" face="Times New Roman" style="font-size:10.0pt;">&nbsp;</font></p>

<p style="margin:0in 0in .0001pt;text-indent:.5in;"><font size="2" face="Times New Roman" style="font-size:10.0pt;">Columbia</font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">  </font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">REIT has the
right to approve certain other aspects of the project, including the property
manager and the management contract, leases with terms that materially differ
from pre-authorized terms, changes to the governing documents of Columbia</font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">  </font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">Project Owner
and certain sales or encumbrances of all or a portion of the project
property.&#160; Columbia</font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">  </font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">REIT also has
rights of access and inspection with respect to the Columbia Project and the
books and records relating to the project.&#160;&#160;
</font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">After completion of the project, </font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">Columbia</font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;"> Project Owner
must maintain the project in good condition and repair and may remove or add
improvements to the project without </font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">Columbia REIT&#146;s </font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">consent only in
limited circumstances. &#160;</font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">Columbia</font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;"> REIT also has
rights with respect to the application of insurance proceeds or condemnation
awards, subject to the rights of </font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">Columbia</font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;"> Senior Lender.</font></p>

<p style="margin:0in 0in .0001pt;text-indent:.5in;"><font size="2" face="Times New Roman" style="font-size:10.0pt;">&nbsp;</font></p>



<p style="margin:0in 0in .0001pt;text-indent:.5in;"><font size="2" face="Times New Roman" style="font-size:10.0pt;">The loan matures on October&nbsp;10,&nbsp;2012.&#160; There is not an extension option for the
maturity date.<b>&#160; </b>Any
unpaid accrued interest on the mezzanine loan is payable on a monthly basis,
first, from a budgeted interest reserve account in the amount of $</font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">3,791,000</font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;"> and, then, from&#160; net cash flow to the extent net cash flow
from the Columbia Project is sufficient to make such payments.&#160; If net cash flow is insufficient to make such
payments, then the interest will continue to accrue and will be payable on a
monthly basis when and to the extent that net cash flow from the Columbia
Project is sufficient to make such payments.&#160;
However, if Columbia REIT does not exercise its option to convert its
mezzanine note into an equity interest in Columbia Investment Partnership, as
described below, then the payment of accrued interest on the mezzanine loan
from funds other than the interest reserve will be subordinate to the payment
of the 9.5% preferred return, compounded annually, payable to the partners in
Columbia Investment Partnership and to the return of their equity investment in
Columbia Investment Partnership (currently, Columbia REIT is the only partner
with a capital contribution eligible for such return).&#160; All accrued and unpaid interest on the
mezzanine loan will be payable upon final maturity of the mezzanine loan.&#160; </font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">Generally no prepayment of
the mezzanine loan may be made except (i)&nbsp;prepayment is permitted 150 days
after the project is completed and (ii)&nbsp;prepayment is required if any of
the interests in the </font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">Columbia Investment Partnership</font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;"> that are the
subject of the Columbia Option (discussed below) are sold (including pursuant
to the exercise of the Columbia Option by Columbia REIT) or there is a sale of
the Columbia Project. </font></p>



<p style="margin:0in 0in .0001pt;text-indent:.5in;"><font size="2" face="Times New Roman" style="font-size:10.0pt;">&nbsp;</font></p>

<p style="margin:0in 0in .0001pt;text-indent:.5in;"><font size="2" face="Times New Roman" style="font-size:10.0pt;">Columbia
REIT received a loan commitment fee of 3% of the loan amount, or $599,000, at
the closing of the loan from the initial advance.</font></p>

<p style="margin:0in 0in .0001pt;text-indent:.5in;"><font size="2" face="Times New Roman" style="font-size:10.0pt;">&nbsp;</font></p>

<p style="margin:0in 0in .0001pt;text-indent:.5in;"><font size="2" face="Times New Roman" style="font-size:10.0pt;">The
mezzanine loan is secured by a lien pursuant to a deed of trust on the Columbia
Project that is subordinate to the lien on the Columbia Project granted to
Columbia</font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">  </font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">Senior Lender.&#160; Columbia REIT has
the right to cure defaults under the senior loan, including the right to
purchase the senior loan.</font></p>

<p style="margin:0in 0in .0001pt;text-indent:.5in;"><font size="2" face="Times New Roman" style="font-size:10.0pt;">&nbsp;</font></p>

<p style="margin:0in 0in .0001pt;text-indent:.55in;"><i><font size="2" face="Times New Roman" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-style:italic;">Management of the Columbia Project</font></i><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">.&#160; Pursuant to the provisions of Columbia
Investment Partnership, Columbia GP generally controls the partnership as
general partner, except for certain major decisions which require the consent
of Columbia REIT, including: (i)&nbsp;changes to the Columbia Project
construction plans or budget, (ii)&nbsp;</font></p>

<p style="margin:0in 0in .0001pt;text-indent:.55in;"><font size="2" face="Times New Roman" style="font-size:10.0pt;">&nbsp;</font></p>

<p align="center" style="margin:0in 0in .0001pt;text-align:center;"><font size="2" face="Times New Roman" style="font-size:10.0pt;">&nbsp;</font></p>

<p align="center" style="margin:0in 0in .0001pt;text-align:center;"><font size="2" face="Times New Roman" style="font-size:10.0pt;">154</font></p>

