<div style="font-family:Times New Roman;">

<p align="center" style="margin:0in 0in .0001pt;text-align:center;"><font size="2" face="Times New Roman" style="font-size:10.0pt;">&nbsp;</font></p>

<p style="margin:0in 0in .0001pt;"><font size="2" face="Times New Roman" style="font-size:10.0pt;">acquiring
material property, (iii)&nbsp;incurring indebtedness or (iv)&nbsp;selling the
Columbia Project, with limited exceptions for each of the foregoing.&#160; Columbia REIT may remove the general partner
for cause under certain circumstances and appoint a successor.</font></p>

<p style="margin:0in 0in .0001pt;text-indent:.55in;"><font size="2" face="Times New Roman" style="font-size:10.0pt;">&nbsp;</font></p>



<p style="margin:0in 0in .0001pt;text-indent:.5in;"><i><font size="2" face="Times New Roman" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-style:italic;">Guarantee.&#160; </font></i><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">Fairfield Residential, a
national developer of multifamily homes, has guaranteed completion of the
development of the Columbia Project in accordance with the plans and
specifications referenced in the mezzanine loan documents if, for any reason
Columbia Project Owner abandons the Columbia Project before its completion or
fails to complete the project on the agreed schedule and pay all construction
costs in full.&#160; Fairfield Residential is
liable for construction cost overruns in excess of the construction
budget.&nbsp; However, this guarantee will be suspended during any period in which
the senior lender does not make senior loan proceeds available to Columbia
Project Owner for any reason other than a default by Columbia Project Owner
that is caused by or in the reasonable control of Columbia Project Owner or a
default by Fairfield Residential, provided that Columbia Project Owner or
Fairfield is making commercially reasonable efforts to cause senior lender to
make such proceeds available or obtain proceeds from a refinancing of the
senior loan.&nbsp; Fairfield Residential has also guaranteed repayment of the
mezzanine loan should Columbia Project Owner become the subject of a bankruptcy
or insolvency proceeding, provided Columbia REIT does not consent in writing to
or otherwise join as a party in such proceeding.&#160; In addition, Fairfield Residential has agreed
to indemnify Columbia REIT against any losses arising as a result of any
environmentally hazardous activity on the property or violation of any
applicable environmental laws relating to the property.&#160; Fairfield Residential directly or indirectly
owns interests in the Columbia Developer Partners. </font></p>



<p style="margin:0in 0in .0001pt;text-indent:.5in;"><font size="2" face="Times New Roman" style="font-size:10.0pt;">&nbsp;</font></p>

<p style="margin:0in 0in .0001pt;text-indent:.5in;"><i><font size="2" face="Times New Roman" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-style:italic;">Columbia Option.&#160; </font></i><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">Columbia REIT
may exercise an option to increase its capital commitment as a limited partner
in Columbia Investment Partnership (the &#147;Columbia Option&#148;).&#160; Columbia REIT may exercise the Columbia
Option, at its discretion, within 90 days of completion of the Columbia
Project.&#160; The purchase price for the
Columbia Option will be the outstanding balance of the mezzanine loan.&#160; If Columbia REIT exercises the Columbia
Option, the outstanding balance of the mezzanine loan will become
second-priority capital contributed to the Columbia Investment Partnership,
entitled to a preferred return of 9.5%, compounded quarterly, until distributed
by the partnership to Columbia REIT, and Columbia REIT&#146;s deemed capital
contributions will be increased accordingly for purposes of items (vi)&nbsp;and
(vii)&nbsp;of the Columbia Investment Partnership distributions discussed
above.</font></p>

<p style="margin:0in 0in .0001pt;text-indent:.5in;"><font size="2" face="Times New Roman" style="font-size:10.0pt;">&nbsp;</font></p>

<p style="margin:0in 0in .0001pt;"><font size="2" face="Times New Roman" style="font-size:10.0pt;">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160; </font><i><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-style:italic;">Columbia
</font></i><i><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-style:italic;">Developer Partners&#146; Put Right</font></i><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">.&#160; The </font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">Columbia </font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">Developer
Partners have a right, commencing on the date of completion of the </font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">Columbia </font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">Project and
continuing until the fourth anniversary of the completion of the </font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">Columbia </font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">Project, to
initiate a procedure to ascertain the fair market value of the </font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">Columbia </font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">Project and,
thus, to ascertain the value of the partnership interests of the </font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">Columbia </font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">Developer
Partners in </font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">Columbia </font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">Investment Partnership.&#160; If such value is not mutually agreed upon by
the </font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">Columbia </font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">Developer Partners and </font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">Columbia </font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">REIT, then such
value would equal the distributions that the </font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">Columbia </font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">Developer
Partners would receive if the </font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">Columbia </font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">Project were
sold at its fair market value, which would be determined by an arbitration
process.&#160; Once such value is agreed upon
or determined, </font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">Columbia </font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">REIT has an option to
purchase the </font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">Columbia </font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">Developer Partners&#146;
interests at that price or to request that the </font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">Columbia </font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">Developer
Partners cause </font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">Columbia </font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">Project Owner to sell the </font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">Columbia </font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">Project for a
price that is not less than the determined fair market value.&#160; The </font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">Columbia </font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">Developer Partners
may then elect whether to proceed with causing a sale of the </font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">Columbia </font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">Project.&#160; If the </font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">Columbia </font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">Developer
Partners do not elect to cause a sale of the </font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">Columbia </font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">Project or are
unable to consummate such a sale, then the </font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">Columbia </font><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">Developer
Partners do not have any additional right to initiate a liquidity event similar
to that described in this paragraph.</font></p>

<p style="margin:0in 0in .0001pt;"><font size="2" face="Times New Roman" style="font-size:10.0pt;">&nbsp;</font></p>

<p style="margin:0in 0in .0001pt;"><font size="2" face="Times New Roman" style="font-size:10.0pt;">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160; </font><i><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-style:italic;">Columbia
REIT&#146;s</font></i><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">  </font><i><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-style:italic;">Call Right</font></i><i><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-style:italic;">.&#160; </font></i><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">If the Columbia
Developer Partners do not exercise their put right described above, then
Columbia REIT has a right, commencing on the fourth anniversary of the date of
completion of the Columbia Project, to initiate a procedure to ascertain the
fair market value of the Columbia Project and, thus, to ascertain the value of
the partnership interests of all of the then-current partners in Columbia
Investment Partnership.&#160; If such value is
not mutually agreed upon by Columbia REIT and the other partners, then such
value would equal the collective distributions that the other partners would
receive if the Columbia Project were sold at its fair market value, which would
be determined by an arbitration process.&#160;
Once such value is agreed upon or determined, Columbia REIT has an
option to purchase the other partners&#146; interests at that price.&#160; If Columbia REIT initiates this procedure but
does not elect to purchase the other parties&#146; interests, then any partner has
the right to initiate buy/sell procedures described below.</font></p>

<p style="margin:0in 0in .0001pt;"><font size="2" face="Times New Roman" style="font-size:10.0pt;">&nbsp;</font></p>

<p style="margin:0in 0in .0001pt;text-indent:.55in;"><i><font size="2" face="Times New Roman" style="font-size:10.0pt;font-style:italic;">Buy/Sell Rights</font></i><font size="2" style="font-size:10.0pt;">.&#160;
Under the limited circumstances described above, any partner in Columbia
Investment Partnership may initiate buy/sell procedures with respect to their
partnership interests.&#160; Under those
procedures, a </font></p>

<p style="margin:0in 0in .0001pt;text-indent:.55in;"><font size="2" face="Times New Roman" style="font-size:10.0pt;">&nbsp;</font></p>

<p align="center" style="margin:0in 0in .0001pt;text-align:center;"><font size="2" face="Times New Roman" style="font-size:10.0pt;">&nbsp;</font></p>

